From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor erosion brush: droplets on the real terrain, weighted
 by the brush (zero outside the radius), no window state

The brush solved the pipe model of the grid solver on a square window around the dab. Its faults (EdErosion.cpp, commit ef5c44a):
- only rain and dissolving were weighted by the brush (RoundWeight / custom weights); settling and the water flow were not, and the window rim was a pinned sink,
  so sediment landed all over the window (changes up to the window edge, a rectangle with a straight edge);
- water, sediment and fluxes of the whole map were kept between dabs but zeroed on the pinned rim of every window and left frozen outside the next one: stripes
  with straight edges at the spacing of the dabs, results that depended on the window size;
- four pipes per cell: a diamond of settled sediment and parallel rills along the axes;
- the thermal step handed material to samples outside the brush; Finish dumped all suspended sediment in the dirty rectangle.

ErodeSession::Dab now releases random droplets (Beyer / Lague: bilinear surface, inertia, speed from the drop) inside the brush; everything a droplet digs or settles is
multiplied by the brush weight of the sample (exactly zero outside the radius; the rain brush up to its reach), a share of the sediment that runs out is put back low in
the brush (conserve), thermal slides only where the whole neighbourhood is under the brush. A droplet's water and load are proportional to its start weight and every droplet
has its own random stream: nothing is a threshold of the weights. Same API: ed_erode_begin takes two more optional keys (inertia, conserve), ed_erode_window / the window
rule is BrushWindow (erode and deposit need no margin now, the rain brush's margin is its reach); Finish returns false (nothing is held back).

Tests (EdErosionTest TestBrushQuality): zero change outside the radius for 3 terrains x 3 radii x 3 falloffs x 3 modes, shaped brush, result independent of the window
margin, radial profile on a plane, isotropy on a round mountain, a stroke over a mountain / ridge (summit, spread, mass, relief, uneven change, no comb), thread count,
map border.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

